[Orange County](https://www.ocgov.com/) - known as “The O.C.” - is known for sunshine and picturesque beaches, and of course, the home of Disneyland.

Under the surface and glamor, Orange County is no stranger to lemon law claims. Anyone can end up with a defective vehicle - and the high population of drivers in the O.C. makes this risk even more dangerous.

At [CLINE APC](/) - a California lemon law firm - we work closely with Orange County residents to resolve lemon claims.

Nearly all consumers affected by a lemon are facing this scenario for the first time. That’s why we want to take this opportunity to educate consumers in Orange County about crucial lemon law facts to help navigate their situation - and earn fair compensation from the manufacturer.

Let’s get into it.

## Orange County: By the Numbers

- Population of Orange County: 3,141,363

- Square Mileage of Orange County: 3,989 sq mi

- Cars Registered in Orange County: 2,884,366

Many of the Southern California counties cover a lot of ground - and Orange County is no exception. Additionally, Orange County does not have the same level of public transportation as other major population centers - namely the Chicago and New York metropolitans.

This means most people in Orange County must rely on themselves for transportation - and the majority of households own vehicles. The result is more vehicles are on the road, and the chances of _defective_ vehicles on the road are greater.

## Requirements: Lemon Law for Cars in Orange County

The first signs of a defect in your vehicle do not automatically qualify it under lemon law for cars. Orange County consumers must be able to prove their vehicle meets the standards of [California’s lemon law](/info/a-comprehensive-guide-to-california-lemon-law). These include:

- The vehicle in question was sold with a valid warranty - either from the manufacturer or the dealership; and

- The defect was reported to the manufacturer or dealership within the terms of the warranty; and

- The defect was not caused by driver error, abuse, or neglect; and

- The manufacturer’s certified repair facility has been given a reasonable number of repair attempts to fix the defect in question; or

- The vehicle has been in the certified repair facility (out of service) for 30 or more total days.

To have a valid [California lemon law claim](/info/everything-you-need-to-know-about-california-lemon-law-claims) in Orange County, you need to have clear, organized records that your vehicle meets the qualifications above. This will be the first order of business when you begin working with an Orange County lemon law attorney.

## First Step: What to Do if You Believe You Have a Lemon

Next on our list of lemon law facts is the general procedure if you suspect you have a vehicle with manufacturer defects.

To reiterate, you’re probably facing this situation for the first time.

You have two immediate options for your first move.

- Contact a lemon law attorney in Orange County

- Contact the auto manufacturer or dealership to report your defect

Now, if you choose option 1, all lemon law attorneys will tell you to do option 2.

The auto manufacturer will document the defect and direct you to a certified facility to begin the repairs process.

A lemon law attorney will tell you the _right_ way to go about reporting the defect - and what to do if it turns into a lemon law case. This is why we always recommend speaking to a lemon lawyer before talking to the manufacturer.

Here’s why:

Automakers and dealerships have legal teams and processes in place to deny lemon law claims. Moreover, they know you’re facing this situation for the first time. Even when you report a defect under the terms of your warranty, they may use trickery to put the blame for the defect on you. An experienced lemon law attorney will make sure you don’t get taken advantage of.

Most California lemon lawyers know you’re new to the process and will be happy to point you in the right direction - even if your situation doesn’t yet qualify for the state’s lemon law procedures.

## Compensation: What You’re Entitled to in an Orange County Lemon Law Claim

If your defective vehicle meets the qualifications of California lemon law for cars, you will need to hire an Orange County lemon law attorney to help build your claim. This claim outlines every last dollar you’re entitled to.

The compensation includes:

- A full vehicle buyback Down payment for the vehicle manufacturer

- All loan payments made

- Remaining balance of the loan

- Official costs associated with the vehicle Sales tax

- Registration

- All incidental costs associated with the lemon Towing fees

- Hotel stays

- Cab/Uber/Lyft expenses

- Meals

- Attorney fees and court costs

If you are loyal to the car brand, you may request a replacement vehicle from the manufacturer, instead of a buyback.

When you hire a lemon attorney, they will work with you to record and organize all the lemon law facts related to your case. This is to ensure no compensation is left on the table.

## Do You Need a Lemon Law Attorney in Orange County?

While you’re not required to hire a California lemon law lawyer to manage your claim, your chances of earning fair compensation without one are very, _very_ slim.

To reiterate, auto manufacturers have very high-powered legal defense teams to fight against lemon law claims. [Negotiating with unsuspecting consumers](/blog/tips-for-negotiating-with-car-dealers-in-a-lemon-case) is easy work for them - and the consumers often end up with a lowball settlement or nothing at all.

An experienced lemon law attorney in Orange County knows all the shady negotiation tactics the automakers use to avoid responsibility for selling defective vehicles. They will make sure you don’t fall victim to these traps.

Most importantly: Many people believe hiring a California lemon law lawyer will be very expensive. What they don’t realize is most lemon attorneys work on a [contingency fee agreement](https://www.caoc.org/?pg=contingencyfees) - because their expenses are paid by the manufacturer as part of the settlement after they win.

This means they won’t charge you ANYTHING out of pocket to take your case. Most provide a free initial consultation to determine the validity of your claim - then decide if it’s worth pursuing. In other words, anyone can [afford to hire a skilled Orange County lemon law attorney](/blog/how-lemon-law-attorneys-work-on-a-contingency-fee-agreement).

